# play — Cline Rules

## Authoritative References
- Architecture: `PLAY_MASTER_PROMPT.md` (project root) — this wins over your training data
- Build order: follow the 19-step sequence in PLAY_MASTER_PROMPT.md exactly
- Current state: Steps 1–3 complete. pe.rs has 17 passing tests.

## Before Writing Any Code
1. Read the relevant existing file first — never assume its contents
2. If touching a module boundary, verify the types it imports/exports compile

## Rust Constraints (non-negotiable)
- No `.unwrap()` or `.expect()` outside `#[cfg(test)]` — use `?` with typed PlayError
- No hardcoded `/proc` or `/sys` paths — all paths use injectable `proc_root`/`sys_root`
- No `unsafe` without a comment justifying it
- `#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]` on all data structs
- Run `cargo check` after every file change before proceeding

## Architecture Rules
- Tweaks are data (Tweak structs in TweakRegistry), never logic in agents
- Orchestrator never contains tweak-specific conditionals
- Rollback manifest written BEFORE any system change, never after
- AMD and NVIDIA GPU code lives in separate impl blocks behind a trait — never mixed in one fn

## Cost Efficiency
- Don't read files you don't need for the current task
- Don't ask clarifying questions when PLAY_MASTER_PROMPT.md has the answer
- Prefer targeted `str_replace` edits over full file rewrites
- One `cargo check` per logical change, not per line
